<details><summary>Click to reveal the one-step proof</summary>
Let $m$ maximize $\pi_i$. For every probability rule $q$, nonnegativity gives $q_i\pi_i\le q_i\pi_m$. Summing yields $\sum_iq_i\pi_i\le\pi_m\sum_iq_i=\pi_m$. Thus a deterministic choice of $m$ is optimal; ties permit any mixture supported on maximizers.
</details>

